#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059508 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a10cafc6-9da7-5ffc-a0c7-686a7638fbd9" :knowledge-point/title "Reducing a 2x2 Augmented Matrix to REF Using Gaussian Elimination"}] :question/id #uuid "0a9e6824-677a-5fae-9867-1701e7d8378f" :question/math-academy-id "e-4697" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071933/assets/67d01790cfbda1f20a23c9e22a64714156485851ce56b2f73e9873db6ef4bed8.png)\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system represented by the matrix." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -2 & -8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -8 & -8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=-\\frac{1}{8}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071933/assets/da9c44be043ad3a15808a9e0dd77636697170047e61b73a0d591bc3581d992fb.png)\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $y=1$ tells us the value of $y.$ Substituting this value into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx+2(1)=0 \n\t\\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad\n\tx=-2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-2$ and $y=1.$ Or, in vector form, $\\left<  -2,1 \\right>.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059509 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "07abc1cc-5794-51a6-bad4-40565eae52be" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 2x2 System of Equations Using Gaussian Elimination"}] :question/id #uuid "1eea81be-26d7-57dd-a622-d66300de7f4f" :question/math-academy-id "e-4698" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071933/assets/a80ecf94bbd4f0ea4b7a860e340039ca80bc5ccd0d2a19503cb9dcc571558976.png)\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071933/assets/ab29f353f00454b6e8eeb490336e2b33d0b2cf6cd47f4d24ac6c8a8f042af628.png)\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 5 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -6 & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=-{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 & -5 \\\\ 1 & -6 & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 & -5 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=-{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -10\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071933/assets/ee5b759f55931cf4935a0763f22c9eb5deedb04f3e247c295aa2a1da09b121b4.png)\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $y=-10$ tells us the value of $y.$ Substituting this value into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx-5(-10)=-5 \n\t\\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad\n\tx=-55.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-55$ and $y=-10.$ Or, in vector form, $\\langle -55,-10 \\rangle.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186306369 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a10cafc6-9da7-5ffc-a0c7-686a7638fbd9" :knowledge-point/title "Reducing a 2x2 Augmented Matrix to REF Using Gaussian Elimination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5d0c7ac1-6ca9-598f-b680-73f9d6ab6ac6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -11\\end{aligned}],$\n$\\,x=19$ and $y=-11$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306371} {:answer/id #uuid "e74442d2-c095-5141-b4bc-4f058c3f434a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 14\\end{aligned}],$\n$\\,x=13$ and $y=14$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306372} {:answer/id #uuid "e2efb109-af41-5b60-bfe1-ab972c90eb29" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 11\\end{aligned}],$\n$\\,x=10$ and $y=11$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306373} {:answer/id #uuid "4b5ee1b4-fd0c-5324-8b7a-eabfeb4505a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 13\\end{aligned}],$\n$\\,x=11$ and $y=13$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306374} {:answer/id #uuid "0d7dc191-62bd-5a73-9efe-0624f55a97ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -16\\end{aligned}],$\n$\\,x=17$ and $y=-16$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306375}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5d0c7ac1-6ca9-598f-b680-73f9d6ab6ac6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -11\\end{aligned}],$\n$\\,x=19$ and $y=-11$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306371} :answer-field/id #uuid "fef724db-7e02-5ac7-859f-fd32828736c3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306370}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6b8bb874-c303-5f60-b208-8afd16f62899" :question/math-academy-id "q-1059" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 8 \\\\ -1 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system represented by the matrix." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 8 \\\\ -1 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+1\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 11\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=-1\\cdot {R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -11\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+y=8 \\\\  & y=-11,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $y=-11$ tells us the value of $y.$ Substituting this value into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx+(-11)=8\\,⇒\\,x=8+11=19.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=19$ and $y=-11.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186374032 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a10cafc6-9da7-5ffc-a0c7-686a7638fbd9" :knowledge-point/title "Reducing a 2x2 Augmented Matrix to REF Using Gaussian Elimination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f7b8eba7-bf5b-584b-97e8-00c5e40e9ff7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{11}{16}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374034} {:answer/id #uuid "b4c35b62-c01f-5354-8208-d5cec20a0def" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{15}{16}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374035} {:answer/id #uuid "a2d647a6-278c-5994-97ee-7870c8878ccd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{17}{16}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374036} {:answer/id #uuid "497a9b0b-c34d-5915-9660-80e41049ff66" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{13}{16}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374037} {:answer/id #uuid "fc38113a-0010-59ce-b64d-9837a0b810fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{9}{16}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374038}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "497a9b0b-c34d-5915-9660-80e41049ff66" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{13}{16}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374037} :answer-field/id #uuid "70639cf9-3345-5368-8a0c-fe1ec47ac05e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374033}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b2cfb536-5e1c-504f-8c3c-31308e0bec9d" :question/math-academy-id "q-1060" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 6 & 8\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form using the standard algorithm for Gaussian elimination, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 6 & 8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=-1\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 5 & 6 & 8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-5\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 16 & 13\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{16}\\cdot {R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{13}{16}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186306376 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a10cafc6-9da7-5ffc-a0c7-686a7638fbd9" :knowledge-point/title "Reducing a 2x2 Augmented Matrix to REF Using Gaussian Elimination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "807b9363-8553-5f5e-93f3-837ca514ec79" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306378} {:answer/id #uuid "db31c201-3ebf-5632-a83f-7785bc6865af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -8 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306379} {:answer/id #uuid "a03c748b-522e-5201-9ffb-4302373be61a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 8 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306380} {:answer/id #uuid "b3ea5721-7f8d-5aab-b3e1-04a3f052bbcb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306381} {:answer/id #uuid "91dfd4c1-1b7f-54f2-ab9f-2be452da8383" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306382}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b3ea5721-7f8d-5aab-b3e1-04a3f052bbcb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306381} :answer-field/id #uuid "56ffb72d-6588-50f8-8e5c-157ca702bdff" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306377}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "dc5530a8-d7bb-5ee6-b842-11178cec4e06" :question/math-academy-id "q-130909" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -8 & 6 \\\\ 3 & -7 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form using the standard algorithm for Gaussian elimination, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & -8 & 6 \\\\ 3 & -7 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -7 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186374039 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a10cafc6-9da7-5ffc-a0c7-686a7638fbd9" :knowledge-point/title "Reducing a 2x2 Augmented Matrix to REF Using Gaussian Elimination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0dc543b6-459a-5fcf-8011-b02a2730bbb9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 7 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}],$ $\\,x=15$ and $y=1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374041} {:answer/id #uuid "a07b071b-1df7-545e-9f12-03b5ebe08484" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 7 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}],$ $\\,x=12$ and $y=-2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374042} {:answer/id #uuid "4b49eddc-f0db-5c41-9338-2b3ca8cdf682" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 7 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}],$ $\\,x=13$ and $y=-1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374043} {:answer/id #uuid "783a60bc-1579-5f45-aecf-c05de1a26b75" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 7 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}],$ $\\,x=5$ and $y=-1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374044} {:answer/id #uuid "ccf8fb30-5ac9-50da-a4bf-09f50dd3b3c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 7 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}],$ $\\,x=12$ and $y=2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374045}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "783a60bc-1579-5f45-aecf-c05de1a26b75" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 7 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}],$ $\\,x=5$ and $y=-1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374044} :answer-field/id #uuid "791e5a06-2eba-5ca0-8882-261a36070737" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374040}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "36655489-58cf-5b95-a28e-946cf05f7596" :question/math-academy-id "q-130910" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 7 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 10 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system represented by the matrix." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 7 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 10 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 7 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=-\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 7 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+7y=-2 \\\\  & y=-1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $y=-1$ tells us the value of $y.$ Substituting this value into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx+7(-1)=-2\\,⇒\\,x=-2+7=5.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=5$ and $y=-1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186374046 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a10cafc6-9da7-5ffc-a0c7-686a7638fbd9" :knowledge-point/title "Reducing a 2x2 Augmented Matrix to REF Using Gaussian Elimination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6a70a0d3-8ddb-54a7-8514-e4a178778c25" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -\\frac{9}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}],$\n$\\,x=-3$ and $y=\\frac{1}{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374048} {:answer/id #uuid "d82abe34-4c80-5f15-abe1-f492d415aa81" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & \\frac{9}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}],$\n$\\,x=3$ and $y=-\\frac{1}{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374049} {:answer/id #uuid "c89f6811-001c-5a38-8de8-4c9bbd39cc4a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -\\frac{9}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1 & -\\frac{17}{2}\\end{aligned}],$\n$\\,x=-1$ and $y=-\\frac{17}{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374050} {:answer/id #uuid "4111a87e-2390-57eb-8123-0cc058bac377" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{17}{2}\\end{aligned}],$\n$\\,x=\\frac{4}{2}$ and $y=\\frac{15}{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374051} {:answer/id #uuid "aa7b35a4-185a-5914-8443-ac0fa4b3c6a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{9}{2}\\end{aligned}],$\n$\\,x=\\frac{1}{2}$ and $y=-\\frac{9}{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374052}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6a70a0d3-8ddb-54a7-8514-e4a178778c25" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -\\frac{9}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}],$\n$\\,x=-3$ and $y=\\frac{1}{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374048} :answer-field/id #uuid "8bffc7d6-a54a-5ece-bc0f-4c9cd4f413b1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374047}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0371d28b-41aa-5288-a97c-eeca95bd4c3f" :question/math-academy-id "q-20461" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -6 & -9 \\\\ 1 & -2 & -4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system represented by the matrix." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & -6 & -9 \\\\ 1 & -2 & -4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -\\frac{9}{2} \\\\ 1 & -2 & -4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -\\frac{9}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x-3y=-\\frac{9}{2} \\\\  & y=\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $y=\\frac{1}{2}$ tells us the value of $y.$ Substituting this value into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx-3(\\frac{1}{2})=-\\frac{9}{2}\\,⇒\\,x=-\\frac{9}{2}+\\frac{3}{2}=-3.\n$$\n\nThus, the solution is $x=-3$ and $y=\\frac{1}{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060126 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "07abc1cc-5794-51a6-bad4-40565eae52be" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 2x2 System of Equations Using Gaussian Elimination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fd273c5e-2100-516a-b1ef-2768979e5d61" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 7 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306398} {:answer/id #uuid "a541204d-7ddb-5553-a580-d02c2fb7b13c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{7}{2} & -\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306399} {:answer/id #uuid "abb243af-5edd-5945-b0a7-d75535ece67b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{7}{2} & -\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306400} {:answer/id #uuid "158cd92e-2094-50c1-a678-7f06cd107c5d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{7}{2} & -\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306401} {:answer/id #uuid "da59ba7a-cac4-51b9-95f0-8e3a0af7c4b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 7 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306402}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "abb243af-5edd-5945-b0a7-d75535ece67b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{7}{2} & -\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306400} :answer-field/id #uuid "853d1717-7599-56c0-8795-a2bd5f10af9f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306397}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a63289e5-22c0-55e8-8542-9af2656af30b" :question/math-academy-id "q-20496" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & 2x+7y=-5 \\\\  & 7x+11y=-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 7 & -5 \\\\ 7 & 11 & -4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 7 & -5 \\\\ 7 & 11 & -4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{7}{2} & -\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ 7 & 11 & -4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-7{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{7}{2} & -\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{27}{2} & \\frac{27}{2}\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=-\\frac{2}{27}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{7}{2} & -\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186374053 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "07abc1cc-5794-51a6-bad4-40565eae52be" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 2x2 System of Equations Using Gaussian Elimination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a66b23d-f2b7-5b5a-a485-c2924bff3dad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{8}{3} & \\frac{22}{3} \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374055} {:answer/id #uuid "e527e797-e39d-578d-bbbc-006ef1d0b4a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{8}{3} & \\frac{22}{3} \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374056} {:answer/id #uuid "f8b782ec-afbf-53ea-9d7e-40ad527aea0a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{8}{3} & \\frac{22}{3} \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374057} {:answer/id #uuid "f65d7876-5637-54ca-b6fb-7afb02938f03" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{8}{3} & \\frac{22}{3} \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374058} {:answer/id #uuid "3a673b7d-d277-5220-9745-5992f0992e76" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{8}{3} & \\frac{22}{3} \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374059}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e527e797-e39d-578d-bbbc-006ef1d0b4a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{8}{3} & \\frac{22}{3} \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374056} :answer-field/id #uuid "e0fa4221-2596-59c8-aef6-c18748848d9f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374054}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "87c26d6c-3cf0-5b9b-ada3-9bbdd3c94fdc" :question/math-academy-id "q-20497" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & 3x+8y=22 \\\\  & 7x-5y=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 8 & 22 \\\\ 7 & -5 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}3 & 8 & 22 \\\\ 7 & -5 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{8}{3} & \\frac{22}{3} \\\\ 7 & -5 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-7{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{8}{3} & \\frac{22}{3} \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{71}{3} & -\\frac{142}{3}\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=-\\frac{3}{71}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{8}{3} & \\frac{22}{3} \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186374060 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "07abc1cc-5794-51a6-bad4-40565eae52be" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 2x2 System of Equations Using Gaussian Elimination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "576f81c5-c3f4-57d4-9f4e-e3d74b15ed79" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{1}{3} & 11 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}],$\n$\\,x=11$ and $y=0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374062} {:answer/id #uuid "bf371e18-f936-5f34-9444-6370fd8e8311" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{1}{3} & 11 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3\\end{aligned}],$\n$\\,x=12$ and $y=-3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374063} {:answer/id #uuid "42b4f57d-b9f8-5f89-95c5-b3ed07cb485c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{1}{3} & 11 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 30\\end{aligned}],$\n$\\,x=1$ and $y=30$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374064} {:answer/id #uuid "dd61b1bc-149a-5ed2-b7ba-83b8912a5cb1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{1}{3} & 11 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}],$\n$\\,x=10$ and $y=3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374065} {:answer/id #uuid "6b48d3af-73c0-5028-a73c-6675071dda87" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{1}{3} & 11 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 6\\end{aligned}],$\n$\\,x=9$ and $y=6$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374066}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "42b4f57d-b9f8-5f89-95c5-b3ed07cb485c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{1}{3} & 11 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 30\\end{aligned}],$\n$\\,x=1$ and $y=30$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374064} :answer-field/id #uuid "2a565768-4632-5861-9fb8-28453cf31453" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374061}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f0075587-5999-58f6-a70b-eea8bfd44ed3" :question/math-academy-id "q-20500" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+\\frac{1}{3}y=11 \\\\  & 3x+\\frac{1}{5}y=9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{1}{3} & 11 \\\\ 3 & \\frac{1}{5} & 9\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{1}{3} & 11 \\\\ 3 & \\frac{1}{5} & 9\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{1}{3} & 11 \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{4}{5} & -24\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=-\\frac{5}{4}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{1}{3} & 11 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 30\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+\\frac{1}{3}y=11 \\\\  & y=30,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $y=30$ tells us the value of $y.$ Substituting this value into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx+\\frac{1}{3}(30)=11\\,⇒\\,x=11-10=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=1$ and $y=30.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186306403 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "07abc1cc-5794-51a6-bad4-40565eae52be" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 2x2 System of Equations Using Gaussian Elimination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "140d9992-5054-56b7-a950-081ea449f8c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{4}{3} \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306405} {:answer/id #uuid "7f53a4ca-9a3e-53f7-8760-a5ed2fe41d61" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{4}{3} \\\\ 0 & 1 & -\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306406} {:answer/id #uuid "40b38b43-671f-57d0-82b2-57e7cb1c052b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{4}{3} \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306407} {:answer/id #uuid "c6f0ee00-58fd-5e72-b7b7-3d98b5938b6d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{4}{3} \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306408} {:answer/id #uuid "f82967e3-bea4-5147-8380-6a1895e8304d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{4}{3} \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306409}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "140d9992-5054-56b7-a950-081ea449f8c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{4}{3} \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306405} :answer-field/id #uuid "85300939-19fc-5c5a-9662-e314a8e5b7f3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306404}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "26bbee69-6c8f-5073-bf18-e5b7229f3605" :question/math-academy-id "q-73538" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & 3x-2y=4 \\\\  & 2x-y=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{4}{3} \\\\ 2 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{4}{3} \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{3} & -\\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=3{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{4}{3} \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186374067 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "07abc1cc-5794-51a6-bad4-40565eae52be" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 2x2 System of Equations Using Gaussian Elimination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6ddfebc2-2d7b-520c-bc95-ae12624edae0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}],$\n$\\,x=1$ and $y=-1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374069} {:answer/id #uuid "9543e6a4-01ee-57eb-ad08-af1a73145a7b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}],$\n$\\,x=-1$ and $y=-2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374070} {:answer/id #uuid "258d1553-4f7f-5bd6-a78f-86ecb0a2ea1e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4\\end{aligned}],$\n$\\,x=-5$ and $y=-4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374071} {:answer/id #uuid "cb134a7c-4374-51e5-807d-50a278d4ad87" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}],$\n$\\,x=7$ and $y=2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374072} {:answer/id #uuid "7ddb2911-b415-5d95-950a-893ae03986c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4\\end{aligned}],$\n$\\,x=11$ and $y=4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374073}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9543e6a4-01ee-57eb-ad08-af1a73145a7b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}],$\n$\\,x=-1$ and $y=-2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374070} :answer-field/id #uuid "f6c329a7-7db1-5c67-8a32-902b842bfc96" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374068}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4e51e1e1-f4ea-594e-af90-cfd7caef02c6" :question/math-academy-id "q-73544" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & 2x-4y=6 \\\\  & 4x-7y=10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 & 6 \\\\ 4 & -7 & 10\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 & 6 \\\\ 4 & -7 & 10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & -7 & 10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x-2y=3 \\\\  & y=-2,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $y=-2$ tells us the value of $y.$ Substituting this value into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx-2(-2)=3\\,⇒\\,x=-1.\n$$\n\nThus, the solution is $x=-1$ and $y=-2.$"}]}
